	When I play NetHack I usually dial in to the local network at 2400
bps.  Under certain conditions, like when a spell is cast upon me or a dragon
breathes on me, for several seconds my character symbol @ gets replaced with
all kinds of other characters (see title).  At first I thought it was a bug,
then I noticed it happening on a regular basis so I thought it must be a
feature (there's a computer programming joke here, I can feel it).  Well, this
has gotten real annoying especially when I'm in a pretty intense combat situ-
ation and my adrenaline's flowing freely and then I have to pause and wait 
several seconds again and Again and AGAIN for this damn sequence to play out.
Is this supposed to be cute?
	My real question is, is there some way to turn this off so I can just
engage in straight combat without the cheap time-devouring character theatrics?
